%% Lifecycle of an entry in procedural memory (skill, playbook, convention)

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Candidate: lesson from a run, with evidence and provenance
    Candidate --> Trial: validated by replay or user approval
    Candidate --> Discarded: contradicted or no evidence
    Trial --> Active: succeeds over N uses, no regressions
    Trial --> Candidate: failed, needs revision
    Active --> Revised: repeated failures or user correction
    Revised --> Trial: patched version, old one kept
    Active --> Deprecated: superseded or unused for long
    Deprecated --> Active: rollback
    Deprecated --> [*]: pruned from the index
    Discarded --> [*]

    note right of Trial: indexed in the manifest, flagged as unproven
    note right of Active: indexed in the manifest, body loaded on demand
